+# Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, on the ground that owner search demonstrates paged prefix search once. Read broadly, that row also declined narrowing the veterinarian directory to one specialty — an attribute the directory already displays against every veterinarian.
+
+The owner asked for that narrowing on 2026-08-31 and decided the row with the request: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-9 as written and decline the request.** Rejected: the owner owns the boundary, and the row's rationale targets free-text search, not narrowing an already-published attribute.
+2. **Drop NG-9 entirely.** Rejected: it would open pet search, visit search, and free-text veterinarian search, none of which was asked for and each of which repeats the owner-search pattern.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing a published listing by a value it already shows is a distinct capability and is in scope. `REQ-VET-003` states it for the veterinarian directory.
+
+The narrowing is bounded to the veterinarian directory and to the specialty a veterinarian holds. Free-text search over veterinarians, pets, and visits stays declined, and this ADR does not open a listing the directory does not already publish.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The two forms of the veterinarian directory become a filtered surface. The machine-readable form gains a requirement for the first time, under the fresh id `REQ-VET-003`.
+- `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn and its id is never reused, so links into the withdrawal still resolve.
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; it is now a decided row. Every other undecided row remains part of it.
+- Filtering arrives as a request contract. No page control is added, which the Open Questions record as a possible later request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
